CAT = "auwhitePlant"; SEG = "PLT"
Q = [
("What does a residual current device (RCD) do?",
 "Cuts power fast if current leaks", ["Boosts voltage for large tools", "Stops leads overheating in sun", "Measures power use on site"],
 "An RCD detects current leaking to earth, for example through a person, and switches off in a fraction of a second. Construction sites must use RCD-protected supply for portable tools."),
("You find an extension lead with cut outer insulation. What should you do?",
 "Tag it out and report it", ["Wrap it in electrical tape", "Use it in dry weather only", "Use it until knock-off"],
 "Damaged leads can expose live wires. Remove the lead from use with an out-of-service tag and report it; only a licensed electrician may repair it."),
("Who may repair the wiring of a faulty power tool?",
 "A licensed electrician", ["Any competent worker", "The site supervisor", "The tool's usual user"],
 "Electrical work, including repairs to wiring, must be done by a licensed electrician. Others must tag the tool out and report it."),
("How should extension leads be run on a construction site?",
 "Up off the ground on stands", ["Through puddles if taped", "Under doors and walkways", "Joined with double adaptors"],
 "Leads should be kept off the ground on lead stands or hooks, away from water, sharp edges and traffic. Piggyback and double adaptors overload circuits."),
("What does the test tag on a power tool show?",
 "When it was last tested", ["Who owns the tool", "Who is allowed to use it", "Its top cutting speed"],
 "The tag records when the tool was inspected and tested, who did it and when the next test is due. Do not use a tool whose test date has passed."),
("You must work near overhead powerlines. What distance must you keep?",
 "The no-go zone set by your state", ["30 cm from any powerline", "1 metre in every state", "None if the lines look well insulated"],
 "Approach distances and no-go zones for overhead powerlines are set by each state and territory and depend on the voltage. Overhead lines are rarely insulated, so never assume they are safe."),
("A worker is in contact with a live wire. What should you do first?",
 "Isolate the power, if safe", ["Pull them away by the arm", "Pour water over them", "Start CPR immediately"],
 "Touching the person while they are live can electrocute you too. Switch off or isolate the supply first, then call 000 and give first aid."),
("Who may remove a personal danger tag from a switch?",
 "Only the person who fitted it", ["Any supervisor on site", "Anyone who needs to use the machine", "The next shift's operator"],
 "A personal danger tag shows that a particular worker is working on the equipment. Only the person who attached it removes it, once they are clear and the job is done."),
("What does an out-of-service tag on equipment mean?",
 "It is faulty; do not use it", ["It is due for a service soon", "It may be used with care", "It belongs to another crew"],
 "An out-of-service tag marks equipment as faulty or unsafe. It must not be used until it is repaired and the tag is removed by an authorised person."),
("Before clearing a jam in a machine, what should you do?",
 "Isolate, lock and tag it out", ["Switch it to its lowest speed", "Ask someone to watch the switch", "Reach in fast while it idles"],
 "Isolate every energy source, fit your personal lock and danger tag, and test that it cannot start. Low speed or a watcher still leaves you exposed."),
("Which of these tasks needs a high risk work licence?",
 "Operating a forklift", ["Using a cordless drill", "Driving the site ute", "Using a nail gun"],
 "Forklift operation is listed high risk work and needs a licence from the regulator. Hand-held power tools and site vehicles need training, not a high risk work licence."),
("Operating a boom-type elevating work platform needs a licence once its boom is:",
 "11 metres or longer", ["5 metres or longer", "8 metres or longer", "15 metres or longer"],
 "A high risk work licence is required for boom-type elevating work platforms with a boom length of 11 metres or more. Smaller units still need training and familiarisation."),
("What is the minimum age to hold a high risk work licence?",
 "18 years", ["16 years", "17 years", "21 years"],
 "Under the model WHS Regulations an applicant for a high risk work licence must be at least 18 years old."),
("A machine guard was removed for cleaning. What must happen next?",
 "Refit it before restarting", ["Run it briefly without it", "Leave it off if you are careful", "Refit it at the end of the day"],
 "Guards stop people contacting moving parts. The machine must not run until the guard is back in place and working."),
("When should plant be checked for faults?",
 "Before each use or shift", ["Only after a breakdown", "Once a month", "Only when it is first delivered"],
 "A pre-start check before each shift or use finds faults such as leaks, damaged guards or failed brakes before they hurt someone. Faulty plant is tagged out and reported."),
("You are asked to use plant you have not been trained on. What should you do?",
 "Say so and ask for training", ["Try it on a small job first", "Watch a video and start", "Have a mate talk you through"],
 "Workers must have the training and any licence needed to use plant safely. Speaking up is part of your duty to take reasonable care."),
("What does a site traffic management plan do?",
 "Separates people and vehicles", ["Sets delivery truck routes interstate", "Lists every driver's licence", "Sets the site's working hours"],
 "A traffic management plan sets routes, exclusion zones, pedestrian paths, speed limits and spotter use so people and moving plant are kept apart."),
("You need to walk past a reversing excavator. What should you do?",
 "Stay clear; get eye contact", ["Walk behind it quickly", "Rely on its reversing alarm", "Wave once and keep walking"],
 "Mobile plant has large blind spots. Stay out of its path and only approach once the operator has seen you and signalled that it is safe."),
("What does a spotter do for mobile plant?",
 "Guides the operator past hazards", ["Records fuel use for each machine", "Inspects plant at the end of day", "Sets the plant's hire schedule"],
 "A spotter watches the area the operator cannot see and guides them clear of people, structures and powerlines, using agreed signals."),
("Where mobile plant operates, pedestrian walkways should be:",
 "Separated by barriers", ["Shared with plant at quiet times", "Through the turning area", "Left unmarked for flexibility"],
 "Physical barriers between walkways and plant routes are the most reliable way to keep people and machines apart."),
("Operating mobile plant fitted with a seatbelt, you should:",
 "Wear it at all times", ["Wear it on public roads only", "Wear it on steep slopes only", "Leave it off to jump clear"],
 "In a rollover the seatbelt keeps the operator inside the rollover protective structure. Operators who try to jump clear are often crushed."),
("May a worker ride on the steps or bucket of a loader?",
 "No, only in a fitted seat", ["Yes, if they hold on tight", "Yes, at walking pace", "Yes, for short trips only"],
 "Passengers may only ride in a seat designed for them. Riders on steps or in buckets are thrown off or crushed."),
("When a crane is lifting, where must you never stand?",
 "Under the suspended load", ["Behind the barricade", "Beside the site office", "At the assembly area"],
 "A load can drop if a sling, hook or crane fails. Keep out of the area under and around the load unless you are the person licensed to handle it."),
("Who is licensed to sling loads and direct a crane operator?",
 "A dogger", ["A forklift operator", "A scaffolder", "A traffic controller"],
 "Dogging is high risk work: a licensed dogger selects and inspects slings, slings the load and directs the crane operator when the load is out of view."),
]
